List of all data entities for any GarageFlow implementation.

############################
System Data Entities (Static)
############################
GARAGE. Definition of the garage. Stores:
•Garage's name
•Total capacity
•Number of floors
•Operating hours
•Front Desk Phone # (Why not?)

FLOORS. Each floor within the garage. Stores:
•Floor number
•Floor name (Examples: null, basement, roof)
•Total spots on the floor
•Available spots
•Garage which it is a floor of (linked to parent garage)

PARKING SPOTS. Definition of the individual spaces on each floor. Stores:
•Spot ID
•Floor (linked to parent floor)
•Spot type (standard, handicap, staff)
•Current Status (available, occupied, broken/out of order)
•Physical location reference (row by column or zone or null(for small garageflow
implementations))

GATES. physical entry and exit hardware. Stores:
•Gate ID
•Gate type (entry or exit)
•current status (open, closed, out of order)
•Garage it belongs to (linked to parent garage)


######################
Transactional Entities (Databases)
######################

TICKETS. A ticket is created at vehicle entry and closed at exit. It represents
 a single parking session. A ticket stores:
•Ticket ID
•Entry timestamp
•Exit timestamp (null until exit)
•Entry gate
•Exit gate (null until exit)
•Assigned parking spot
•Vehicle ID
•Ticket status: active, closed, lost, voided
•Duration (calculated on close)
•Total fee owed (calculated on close)

PAYMENTS. Records the financial transaction tied to a closed ticket. Stores:
•Payment ID
•Linked ticket ID
•Amount charged
•Payment method (cash, card, mobile/app)
•Payment timestamp
•Payment status (paid, pending, failed, refunded).
 
RESERVATIONS. Pre-booked parking sessions. Stores:
•Reservation ID
•Customer ID
•Vehicle ID
•Start datetime
•End datetime
•Reservation status(confirmed, cancelled, fulfilled, expired)
•Creation timestamp
•Fee quoted at time of booking.

OCCUPANCY LOG. A time stamped log of spot level status changes. Stores:
Storing parking data in this database lets us get live information
and parking analytics / reports from the samespot.
A time-series audit log of spot-level status changes.
Each record stores: 
•Spot ID
•Timestamp of the change
•Spot Became free or spot became occupied.

###############################
Customer Information (Databases)
################################

CUSTOMERS. Registered users. Being a registered user is only needed for
reservations. Stores:
•Customer ID
•Customer personal information:
	•name
	•email
	•phone number
	•date account created
	•account status (active/suspended/deleted)

VEHICLES. Tracks vehicles associated with tickets and reservations. Stores:
•Vehicle ID
•License plate
	•State / region
	•Vehicle type (car / motorcycle/ truck)
•Customer ID (possibly null)

#######################
Operations / Analytics (Logs and important references)
#######################

PRICING RULES. Defines are parking fees are calculated. Each parking ID relates
to a unique payment structure. Each rate object stores:
•Rate ID
•Rate name (standard, weekend, event)
•applicable hours
•Pricing model (flat / hourly / special)
•Description (text)
•Program (points to a function that takes an entry and exit timestamp
and returns a number / fee)

SYSTEM EVENTS. Logs system level actions for security and debugging. Any
part of the system can create an entry to System Events. Stores:
•Event ID (Could be anything but should be unique and traceable. Examples. sensor
fault, ticket voided, manual override took place)
•Source 
•Description field (string / text box)

STAFF. Internal users. Stores:
•Operator ID
•Name
•Role (admin / attendant)
•Login credentials
